## Founding & History
Meander Valley Vineyard was established in 2021 when Bron Dance and Jade Nicholls, along with their children, relocated from Melbourne to Tasmania's Meander Valley. The property was previously known as Three Willows Vineyard and had been in operation for 25 years before their acquisition. The new owners undertook a strategic refresh and name change, drawing on the idea of the Meander Valley as a destination. They have since expanded the cellar door, added a wood-fired pizza oven, and built new accommodation.

## People
The current owners of Meander Valley Vineyard are Bron Dance and Jade Nicholls. Bron manages the cellar door, accommodation, and marketing, while Jade tends to the vines and maintains the grounds. Winemaker Andrew Gaman crafts the wines using only estate-grown fruit. The family lives on-site and is actively involved in all aspects of the business.

## Vineyard & Site
The vineyard spans 15 acres, with five acres under vine. It is located in Red Hills, Tasmania, approximately 35 minutes from both Devonport and Launceston. The site benefits from clean air, fertile soils, and pristine water, surrounded by the Western Tiers and Cradle Mountain. Four varietals are grown on site: Chardonnay, Pinot Gris, Pinot Noir, and Baco Noir. Baco Noir is noted as a rare variety in Australia, bottled only by Meander Valley. The vineyard focuses on cool-climate viticulture.

## Cellar Door Experience
The cellar door is open Thursday to Sunday from 11:30 AM to 4:30 PM. Bookings are recommended, especially for groups and wine tastings, which are available outside peak service periods. The cellar door offers a relaxed and welcoming atmosphere for guided tastings, wines by the glass or bottle, and is dog-friendly for leashed pets. Visitors can enjoy the picturesque surroundings, including views of the Western Tiers and Cradle Mountain. The vineyard also participates in the Tasmanian Mixed Dozen freight scheme, allowing visitors to ship purchased wines home.

## Food & Hospitality
Wood-fired pizza is available Thursday, Friday, and Saturday from 12 PM to 3 PM. A "build your own platter" option, featuring local Tasmanian produce, is available every day from 11:30 AM to 3:30 PM. Sample pizza menu items include Ginseng Spice and Mozzarella, Marinated Lamb with Caramelised Onion, Roasted Mushroom, Baby Spinach and Danish Fetta, Tandoori Chicken, and Game Keeper. Gluten-free and vegan options are available. The cellar door is suitable for intimate gatherings, seating up to 45 guests or 65 for cocktail events. Luxury glamping accommodation, known as Vintners Rest, is available on site, featuring two canvas tents with heated flooring, kitchenettes, wood-fired hot tubs, and decks facing the vines.

## Awards & Recognition
Meander Valley Vineyard was recognized as the leading Fine Dining Restaurant in Meander Valley Council in 2026, achieving a quality score of 95%+ and representing the top 1% of Australian businesses. Their Pinot Gris has won awards. The Halliday Wine Companion has rated their Pinot Noir 2023 at 93 points (silver) and their Sparkling Rosé Non Vintage at 93 points (silver). The Pinot Gris 2023 also received 92 points (silver).

## Sustainability & Certifications
The vineyard is family-owned and operated with a focus on sustainability and a deep connection to the land. Meander Valley Vineyard holds Quality Tourism Accreditation and Sustainable Tourism Accreditation by ATIC.

## Visiting Practical Info
The address is 46 Montana Road, Red Hills, Tasmania, 7304, Australia. It is located approximately 5 minutes from Deloraine. The vineyard is a 35-minute drive from both Devonport and Launceston. The phone number for the cellar door is 0455 224 414. The official website is http://meandervalleyvineyard.com.au/. The vineyard is dog-friendly.

## Notable / Distinctive
Meander Valley Vineyard is distinctive for being a family-owned and operated vineyard that underwent a "vine-change" by its current owners, Bron Dance and Jade Nicholls, in 2021. They are one of the few wineries in Australia to bottle Baco Noir, a rare cold-hardy French/American hybrid grape. The vineyard offers luxury glamping accommodation, Vintners Rest, with features like heated flooring and wood-fired hot tubs overlooking the vines. Their branding, featuring luminescent-yellow bottle tops and minimalist labels with vertical text and empathetic colors, is also noted as distinctive. The cellar door offers wood-fired pizzas and platters made with local Tasmanian produce. The vineyard is situated on the Tasting Trail, surrounded by other local producers.

